
This demo trains eigenvectors with short amount of 3 body's trajectories and forecasts their longer trajectories.
Unlike other demos, I think there's no need to look for another Hilbert space other than the current one.

I'm not astrophycist, so I'm not sure for every details 
but the current result represents forecasting the 3 body's trajectory
without having information of 3 body's masses. Therefore, if the circumstances doesn't provide their mass information, this might be useful.

Expanding the current version to N-body simulation is on going so that it becomes more easy to use and generic.
